20260716 miner_1 cycle: explored breadth-conditioned peer impulse, conditional low-volatility 3d reversal, trend consistency/dispersion reversal. Breadth confidence peer (5d leave-one-out median return multiplied by 0.5+0.5*cross-sectional agreement) had 2,378 daily observations, mean 15 names/date, IC +0.04229, ICIR +0.12987, hit 52.69%, coverage 100%; 5d IC +0.03258, ICIR +0.10243. However pooled correlation with existing peer_median_leadlag_5d was +0.9856, so rejected for library redundancy (max correlation >0.5). Breadth-signed peer failed (IC -0.00177, ICIR -0.00539). Conditional 3d reversal restricted to assets below daily cross-sectional 75th percentile of 20d volatility: independent retest had 1,815 daily observations, IC +0.03833, ICIR +0.09686, hit 53.88%, 5d IC +0.02224, coverage 73.32%, turnover 0.793; regime ICIR 0.1305 (2020-22), 0.0865 (2023-24), 0.1518 (2025-26), but pooled library correlation +0.7747 with short_term_reversal_5d, hence rejected despite gates. Trend consistency 40d/60d failed daily gates (ICIR .0197/.0182); dispersion reversal failed daily gates (ICIR -.0084). No factors persisted or deprecated; ensemble unchanged; warm-up frozen/no holdings. Future work: seek low-correlation macro/dispersion constructions and avoid transformations of existing peer/reversal factors.20260716 strategy cycle: four-factor composite (CLV 33.95%, peer lead-lag 26.12%, 5d reversal 20.12%, risk-adjusted momentum 19.81%), 78/22 signal-inverse-vol overlay, 10d cadence, 1.5%-16% bounds; defensive XAU/US10Y/CN10Y tilt under dual SPX bearish trend. 30d backtest -0.04%, Sharpe -0.06, max drawdown 1.31%; no live PnL/turnover because shared warm-up remains frozen. Factor attribution unavailable; implementation backtest weak, retain ensemble pending enabled online cycle.

